{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"answers\":[{\"question_id\":\"Q015_artifact_tag_not_homology\",\"answer\":\"In SCOPe 2.08, PDB 1a14 chain H is split into the biological VH domain d1a14h1, residues H:9-111, and the short second segment d1a14h2, residues H:1-8. d1a14h2 is not another immunoglobulin domain: it is a synthetic N-terminal tag in the SCOPe artifact class l, with lineage Artifacts -> Tags fold l.1 -> Tags superfamily l.1.1 -> Tags family l.1.1.1 -> N-terminal Tags -> Synthetic. Therefore similarity to d1a14h2 should not be counted as evidence of biological protein homology, should not be used to transfer the VH family/superfamily/fold assignment of d1a14h1, and should not be treated as a valid homologous structural template segment; SCOPe explicitly marks class-l artifact records as artificial sequence artifacts for which similarity does not imply biological homology.\",\"evidence_used\":[\"mcp__scope.get_scop_domains: /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h1\",\"mcp__scope.get_scop_domains: /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h1/parents\",\"mcp__scope.get_scop_domains: /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h2\",\"mcp__scope.get_scop_domains: /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h2/parents\",\"mcp__scope.get_scop_domains: /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1a14h2/homology\"]}]}"}}
